the-firm-as-one-program-83 = unlines (cons "- **N2** The bridge to the rationality claim." (cons (quoted (cons "  P1 (Observation fibers: what a reading warrants, and when a participant is safe to act (§1, §10.4))'s warrant is the formal form of " (cons "the rational actor cannot be incorrect" (cons ", and that is what C17 (Disagreements resolve on a presented shared basis ([P1], plus common ground)) runs on. A rational actor concludes P only when it holds a construction of P over every history compatible with what it observed. Where no such construction exists it concludes nothing, so it is never wrong. The language therefore marks exactly what is amenable to rule-based logic: what is derived, what is observed, and what is a stated premise. English could always carry perfect inference for the rational; the language makes that discipline executable and shared. See [P1: Observation fibers: what a reading warrants, and when a participant is safe to act (hyperactivity v31 §1, §10.4)], [C17: Disagreements resolve on a presented shared basis ([P1], plus common ground)]." nil)))) nil))
